{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וה'", :translit "ve-H'", :gloss "and YHWH"} {:he "פקד", :translit "pakad", :gloss "remembered/visited"} {:he "אם לא תתן לה עתה בן א\"כ תאחר את הקץ שגזרת", :translit "im lo titen lah atah ben az t'acher et ha-ketz she-gazarat", :gloss "if You do not give her a son now then You delay the End that You decreed"} {:he "ת' שנה משיהיה לו זרע והוא בן מאה עתה", :translit "tav shanah mi-sheyihyeh lo zera ve-hu ben me'ah atah", :gloss "400 years from when he has seed, and he is now one hundred years old"} {:he "ואם טהורה היא ונקתה ונזרעה זרע", :translit "ve-im tehorah hi veniktah venizra'ah zera", :gloss "and if she is pure, she shall be cleared and sown with seed"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Interprets וה׳ as 'He and His court' — anytime וה׳ appears, it signals God acting through a judicial framework with advocates and prosecutors arguing."} {:kind :other, :note "Calculates 400 years of Egyptian exile from Genesis 15:13 as beginning when Isaac is born, since Abraham is 100 at this point and Isaac is the seed."} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["נתעברו מביאת איסור מאביהן" "לא תתעבר מאברהם" "נסתרה עם אבימלך"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase וה׳ פקד את שרה marks the moment God's promise of a son to Abraham and Sarah is fulfilled (Genesis 17:19, 18:10, 18:14). The chronology of the Egyptian exile — 400 years (Genesis 15:13) — is reckoned from Isaac's birth, since Isaac is the seed from whom the nation descends. The law of the suspected adulteress in Numbers 5:11-31 includes the verse ואם טהורה היא ונקתה ונזרעה זרע (Numbers 5:28), which the Rabbis read as a guarantee of conception for the vindicated woman.", :sources ["Genesis 15:13" "Genesis 17:19" "Genesis 18:10" "Genesis 18:14" "Numbers 5:28"]}} {:quotes [{:he "פקד את שרה", :translit "pakad et sarah", :gloss "He remembered Sarah"} {:he "אף כל העקרות פקד", :translit "af kol ha-akarot pakad", :gloss "He also remembered all the barren women"}], :mechanisms [{:kin